            {
              "id": "TF-K8S-007",
              "name": "PodSharesTheHostPidOrIpcNamespace",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Pod shares the host PID or IPC namespace"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Sharing hostPID lets the container see and signal every process on the node, and read secrets from other processes' /proc/<pid>/environ. Sharing hostIPC exposes shared memory segments belonging to other workloads."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Sharing hostPID lets the container see and signal every process on the node, and read secrets from other processes' /proc/<pid>/environ. Sharing hostIPC exposes shared memory segments belonging to other workloads. **Remediation:** Remove hostPID and hostIPC. ```yaml spec: hostPID: false hostIPC: false ``` CWE: CWE-668 \u00b7 MITRE: T1057, T1611 \u00b7 CIS: 5.2.2, 5.2.3 \u00b7 NIST: SC-4",
                "markdown": "Sharing hostPID lets the container see and signal every process on the node, and read secrets from other processes' /proc/<pid>/environ. Sharing hostIPC exposes shared memory segments belonging to other workloads.\n\n**Remediation:** Remove hostPID and hostIPC.\n\n```yaml\nspec:\n  hostPID: false\n  hostIPC: false\n```\n\nCWE: CWE-668 \u00b7 MITRE: T1057, T1611 \u00b7 CIS: 5.2.2, 5.2.3 \u00b7 NIST: SC-4"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
