            {
              "id": "TF-K8S-008",
              "name": "ContainerAddsDangerousLinuxCapabilities",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Container adds dangerous Linux capabilities"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Container shop/sidecar-agent adds capabilities SYS_ADMIN, NET_RAW. SYS_ADMIN is close to full root; SYS_PTRACE allows reading memory of other processes; NET_ADMIN permits traffic redirection and ARP spoofing; SYS_MODULE allows loading kernel modules, which is a direct host takeover."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Container shop/sidecar-agent adds capabilities SYS_ADMIN, NET_RAW. SYS_ADMIN is close to full root; SYS_PTRACE allows reading memory of other processes; NET_ADMIN permits traffic redirection and ARP spoofing; SYS_MODULE allows loading kernel modules, which is a direct host takeover. **Remediation:** Drop ALL, then add back only the minimum. ```yaml securityContext: capabilities: drop: [\"ALL\"] add: [\"NET_BIND_SERVICE\"] # example only ``` CWE: CWE-250 \u00b7 MITRE: T1611 \u00b7 CIS: 5.2.8, 5.2.9 \u00b7 NIST: AC-6, CM-7",
                "markdown": "Container shop/sidecar-agent adds capabilities SYS_ADMIN, NET_RAW. SYS_ADMIN is close to full root; SYS_PTRACE allows reading memory of other processes; NET_ADMIN permits traffic redirection and ARP spoofing; SYS_MODULE allows loading kernel modules, which is a direct host takeover.\n\n**Remediation:** Drop ALL, then add back only the minimum.\n\n```yaml\nsecurityContext:\n  capabilities:\n    drop: [\"ALL\"]\n    add: [\"NET_BIND_SERVICE\"]   # example only\n```\n\nCWE: CWE-250 \u00b7 MITRE: T1611 \u00b7 CIS: 5.2.8, 5.2.9 \u00b7 NIST: AC-6, CM-7"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "cwe/CWE-250",
                  "mitre/T1611",
                  "pack:k8s-workload",
                  "privilege",
                  "security",
                  "stride/E",
                  "stride/T"
                ],
                "security-severity": "6.4",
                "precision": "very-high"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "TF-NET-009",
              "name": "NodeportServiceExposesTheWorkloadOnEveryNode",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "NodePort service exposes the workload on every node"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A NodePort opens the port on every node in the cluster. Whether that is internet-reachable depends entirely on node security groups, which are usually managed by a different team than the manifest -- so this is exposure you cannot verify from the manifest alone."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "A NodePort opens the port on every node in the cluster. Whether that is internet-reachable depends entirely on node security groups, which are usually managed by a different team than the manifest -- so this is exposure you cannot verify from the manifest alone. **Remediation:** Prefer ClusterIP behind an Ingress; if NodePort is required, restrict node security groups. CWE: CWE-668 \u00b7 MITRE: T1133 \u00b7 NIST: SC-7",
                "markdown": "A NodePort opens the port on every node in the cluster. Whether that is internet-reachable depends entirely on node security groups, which are usually managed by a different team than the manifest -- so this is exposure you cannot verify from the manifest alone.\n\n**Remediation:** Prefer ClusterIP behind an Ingress; if NodePort is required, restrict node security groups.\n\nCWE: CWE-668 \u00b7 MITRE: T1133 \u00b7 NIST: SC-7"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
