            {
              "id": "TF-K8S-017",
              "name": "ServiceAccountTokenAutomountedButUnusedApiAccess",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Service account token automounted but unused API access"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "automountServiceAccountToken is unset, so a projected API token is mounted at /var/run/secrets/kubernetes.io/serviceaccount. If the workload does not call the Kubernetes API, this token is pure attack surface -- it is the first thing post-exploitation tooling looks for."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "automountServiceAccountToken is unset, so a projected API token is mounted at /var/run/secrets/kubernetes.io/serviceaccount. If the workload does not call the Kubernetes API, this token is pure attack surface -- it is the first thing post-exploitation tooling looks for. **Remediation:** Set automountServiceAccountToken false unless the pod calls the API server. ```yaml spec: automountServiceAccountToken: false ``` CWE: CWE-522 \u00b7 MITRE: T1528 \u00b7 CIS: 5.1.6 \u00b7 NIST: AC-6",
                "markdown": "automountServiceAccountToken is unset, so a projected API token is mounted at /var/run/secrets/kubernetes.io/serviceaccount. If the workload does not call the Kubernetes API, this token is pure attack surface -- it is the first thing post-exploitation tooling looks for.\n\n**Remediation:** Set automountServiceAccountToken false unless the pod calls the API server.\n\n```yaml\nspec:\n  automountServiceAccountToken: false\n```\n\nCWE: CWE-522 \u00b7 MITRE: T1528 \u00b7 CIS: 5.1.6 \u00b7 NIST: AC-6"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
